WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.860
So recently I came across
this tweet by Andrej Karpathy

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.440
where he talks about how he uses
AI to learn anything faster.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.840
Specifically, the part that really
stood out to me was he was using

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.500
AI to create visual explainers
for things that he was learning.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.299
So I decided to try this out,
and it's actually pretty insane.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:18.420
If you haven't tried out
the latest AI models,

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.120
there's been some pretty major
advancements just in the past month.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.600
So now models are good enough where
rather than just spitting out a

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.140
bunch of text and you have to read
through it to understand something,

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.140
it can just show you and explain
it to you with audio and visual.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.340
Let me show you a few examples that
I made The model boils everything

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.860
down to one list of numbers, a
score for every word it knows.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.700
Then it picks- Loaded ships
leave in one lane two miles wide.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.940
Empty ships come in through another
with a two-mile buffer between them.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.920
The molecule is shaped enough
like testosterone to slide

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.580
into the enzyme's pocket,
but once inside, it jams.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.640
It's pretty crazy when you see how
much progress AI video has come

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.280
in just the past few months, where
earlier this year it was still

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:05.819
pretty much slop and not really that
useful or watchable or reliable.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.780
But now it can actually create
very detailed explainers with

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.820
mathematical concepts, with
graphs, with really detailed,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.220
intricate parts that it
can show you in a video.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.920
And also the audio models now
are so good that it basically

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.160
sounds like a real person
explaining something to you.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.200
All right, so in this video
I'm gonna show you the full

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.520
workflow that I use to set this
up, and once you set it up,

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.640
any AI that you use, whether
it's Claude or ChatGPT,

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:33.820
can create these videos automatically
and just send it to you in the chat.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.600
This video is also
sponsored by Higgsfield,

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.000
which is an all-in-one platform for
creating audio and video with AI.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.220
I've personally been a paying user since
earlier this year, and I think they're

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.640
really pushing the boundaries of what
is possible with AI video creation.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.440
For example, they've made full-on feature
length movies using their platform,

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.420
and they're also hosting competitions
and sponsoring filmmakers

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.160
to use their platform and to
make short films or movies.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.200
Some of the results are really quite
mind-blowing, and if you haven't

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.640
been paying attention to AI video,
you probably think it's still slop

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.140
