There are a lot of ways that
you could reduce the cost,

00:13:57.564 --> 00:14:02.744
so for example, if you already have
a Claude or OpenAI subscription,

00:14:02.924 --> 00:14:05.184
you could just have it
be part of your usage.

00:14:05.264 --> 00:14:08.804
All the diagrams could be generated,
programmatically on your computer,

00:14:08.884 --> 00:14:11.744
and maybe even the visuals could
be part of the subscription.

00:14:11.824 --> 00:14:15.424
At least with Haxfield, like creating an
image or creating a few images for each

00:14:15.504 --> 00:14:19.564
generation, it doesn't really cost that
much, considering what you're getting.

00:14:19.644 --> 00:14:22.104
But I do think that the cost
is really only temporary,

00:14:22.184 --> 00:14:25.324
and over time they will go down and
become cheaper and cheaper to the

00:14:25.404 --> 00:14:27.924
point where we can just run them
locally on our phones or computers.

00:14:28.004 --> 00:14:32.484
But yeah, besides the cost, the second
limitation I would say is the time.

00:14:32.564 --> 00:14:36.364
Right now, each generation could still
take maybe five to ten minutes to

00:14:36.444 --> 00:14:40.904
generate, depending on how complex it
is that the visual explainer it is.

00:14:41.324 --> 00:14:44.244
So it really makes the most
sense for something that

00:14:44.324 --> 00:14:47.604
it can do in the background
or do on a schedule.

00:14:47.684 --> 00:14:52.144
So for me, it works really
well with the daily brief or

00:14:52.324 --> 00:14:55.664
the weekly or monthly analysis
videos I have it make.

00:14:55.744 --> 00:14:59.204
I'm really looking forward to
in the near future where it can

00:14:59.284 --> 00:15:03.084
generate these videos almost
instantaneously in real time,

00:15:03.164 --> 00:15:06.404
so instead of a voice
call with your AI agent,

00:15:06.484 --> 00:15:09.884
it's like a video call where you can
just see different things moving around.

00:15:10.424 --> 00:15:13.784
I think that will really
be quite fun and exciting.

00:15:13.864 --> 00:15:16.224
The last limitation I
wanna share is that this

00:15:16.304 --> 00:15:19.464
is really not a replacement
for true learning.

00:15:19.704 --> 00:15:24.464
And, this could be more of a reminder
than it is a limitation, but it's

00:15:24.544 --> 00:15:28.804
important to remember that with true
learning, you need to have active recall,

00:15:28.884 --> 00:15:33.244
and you need to have actual application
of the things that you're learning.

00:15:33.324 --> 00:15:36.204
I think it's important to just remember
to not fall down the rabbit hole of just

00:15:36.284 --> 00:15:39.804
consuming more information or generating
more information for you to learn

00:15:39.884 --> 00:15:44.164
instead of actually using that information
and applying it in your own life.

00:15:44.244 --> 00:15:47.444
Obviously, this is less applicable if
you're just telling your AI to create

00:15:47.524 --> 00:15:52.084
